<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Franco-Dahomean War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Franco-Dahomean War was fought in 1890 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/behanzin">Behanzin</a>, over French claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotonou">Cotonou</a> and protection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-novo">Porto-Novo</a>. Dahomean forces, including the women soldiers, attacked French positions at Cotonou and Atchoupa. The war ended in October 1890 with a treaty recognising French positions on the coast in return for an annual payment, but conflict resumed in 1892.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-franco-dahomean-war.jpg" alt="First Franco-Dahomean War" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dahomey_amazon2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
